      {
        "id": 129710,
        "name": "Mezike",
        "username": "Mezike",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/m/c6cbf5/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2015-01-29T14:18:08.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>What constitutes a prominent delay then? It's only been in stores for literally two days. If they get the VAT number through in the next few days and ship out then it doesn't really matter. If we're still hanging on another couple of weeks down the line, then I agree that it would be getting a bit too much.</p><p>Regarding shipping prices, even&nbsp; though they will have a better rate as a business the costs to ship from 'murica to the UK are eye wateringly expensive. They did increase the cost after they got their fingers burnt on the first KS but I believe they were still claiming a loss through subsidies. Might be I'm wrong about it, but if they can ship internationally for exactly what they charged then they must have a massive discount rate going on there! I don't blame them for trying something new and cheaper, but like I mentioned way up the thread there must be a tipping point where they have to write the endeavour off on this occasion; I just don't think we've reached that point <em>yet</em>. In any case, I totally support people venting if they are upset about the situation, I might not be particularly bothered but I know a lot of others are.</p>",
        "post_number": 24,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:04:42.146Z",
